Here is the commit message:
net/mlx5e: alloc the correct size for indirection_rqt

The cited patch allocated the wrong size for the indirection_rqt table,
fix that.

Fixes: 2119bda642c4 ("net/mlx5e: allocate 'indirection_rqt' buffer dynamically")
CC: Arnd Bergmann <arnd@arndb.de>
Signed-off-by: Saeed Mahameed <saeedm@nvidia.com>

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by allocating the wrong size for the `indirection_rqt` table using `kzalloc`, which did not account for the size of each element, leading to potential memory allocation issues and incorrect behavior in the program. The use of `kcalloc` in the fix correctly allocates memory based on the number of elements and their size, ensuring proper memory management and initialization.

Here is the patch:

 static int mlx5e_hairpin_fill_rqt_rqns(struct mlx5e_hairpin *hp, void *rqtc)
 {
-	u32 *indirection_rqt, rqn;
 	struct mlx5e_priv *priv = hp->func_priv;
 	int i, ix, sz = MLX5E_INDIR_RQT_SIZE;
+	u32 *indirection_rqt, rqn;

-	indirection_rqt = kzalloc(sz, GFP_KERNEL);
+	indirection_rqt = kcalloc(sz, sizeof(*indirection_rqt), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!indirection_rqt)
 		return -ENOMEM;

 	mlx5e_build_default_indir_rqt(indirection_rqt, sz,
 				      hp->num_channels);

 	for (i = 0; i < sz; i++) {
 		ix = i;
 		if (priv->rss_params.hfunc == ETH_RSS_HASH_XOR)
 			ix = mlx5e_bits_invert(i, ilog2(sz));
 		ix = indirection_rqt[ix];
 		rqn = hp->pair->rqn[ix];
 		MLX5_SET(rqtc, rqtc, rq_num[i], rqn);
 	}

 	kfree(indirection_rqt);
 	return 0;
 }



